WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.035
- Decker.

00:00:02.035 --> 00:00:05.305 align:start position:0%
Agent Jackson, you'll be working
with him on this mission.

00:00:05.305 --> 00:00:08.141
- Agent Jackson, let's
get one thing straight,

00:00:08.141 --> 00:00:12.345
I don't like orders and I
don't play by the rules.

00:00:12.345 --> 00:00:13.913
I trust you heard of me?

00:00:13.913 --> 00:00:15.482
- Actually, no, I haven't.

00:00:15.482 --> 00:00:16.316
- Ohhh.

00:00:17.283 --> 00:00:18.518
Hubba hubba.

00:00:18.518 --> 00:00:23.390
♪ Well, I want you
but I don't need ya ♪

00:00:24.124 --> 00:00:26.426
(poppy club music)

00:00:28.061 --> 00:00:29.329
- That's right,
Sergeant Krandle,

00:00:29.329 --> 00:00:30.597
United States Army recruiter.

00:00:30.597 --> 00:00:31.831
How y'all doing?

00:00:31.831 --> 00:00:33.500
This my associate
Sergeant Grampacks.

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:36.436 align:start size:84% position:16%
Yeah.
- Huh, huh, huh, huh.

00:00:36.436 --> 00:00:37.670
Nice beat, gentlemen.

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:39.205
- We wanna talk to
you about your future

00:00:39.205 --> 00:00:41.374
and where you fit in the
United States Army y'all.

00:00:41.374 --> 00:00:43.009
- In case you haven't heard,

00:00:43.009 --> 00:00:44.611
we're asking and you're telling.

00:00:44.611 --> 00:00:45.979
- That's right, no
restrictions, man.

00:00:45.979 --> 00:00:47.747 align:start size:84% position:16%
You gon' be surrounded
by dudes all day.

00:00:47.747 --> 00:00:49.215
Y'all can exercise together.

00:00:49.215 --> 00:00:50.483
You can shower together.

00:00:50.483 --> 00:00:52.385 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Talking bout soap,
water, the works.

00:00:52.385 --> 00:00:53.486
- Now, I know what
you're thinking,

00:00:53.486 --> 00:00:55.055
the army's dangerous,

00:00:55.055 --> 00:00:57.057
but the fact of the matter
is everything's dangerous.

00:00:57.057 --> 00:00:59.059 align:start size:84% position:16%
- All depends on
what your definition

00:00:59.059 --> 00:01:00.460
of the word danger is.

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:01.428
- Uh-oh, yeah.

00:01:01.428 --> 00:01:02.595
- What!
- What!

00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:07.500 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Oh, here we go.
- Oh, we gotta friend.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:08.668
- Hey, Navy already got him.

00:01:08.668 --> 00:01:09.903
(Key chuckling)

00:01:09.903 --> 00:01:11.404
But you're better
off in the Army,

00:01:11.404 --> 00:01:13.406
cause we gon' get you in the
best shape in your whole life.

00:01:13.406 --> 00:01:14.340
- Whoo!

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:15.108
Talking about a six pack.

00:01:15.108 --> 00:01:16.042
- Blip!

00:01:16.042 --> 00:01:16.776
- Gon' give you an eight pack.

00:01:16.776 --> 00:01:18.011
- Sklimp!

00:01:18.011 --> 00:01:18.678 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Hey, we'll even
give you a jet pack!

00:01:18.678 --> 00:01:19.946
(Key laughing)

00:01:19.946 --> 00:01:20.747
- That's a joke, man, he
a joker, he a funny guy.

00:01:20.747 --> 00:01:21.414
We ain't got jet packs.

00:01:21.414 --> 00:01:22.248
- Whoa, whoaaaa!

00:01:22.248 --> 00:01:23.917
- Oh, that's my cut.

00:01:25.452 --> 00:01:27.420
- Go ahead, go ahead.

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:28.321
Hey, hey, hey.

00:01:28.321 --> 00:01:29.322
You got to isolate,

00:01:29.322 --> 00:01:30.256
then isolate

00:01:30.256 --> 00:01:31.624
then is-o-late.

00:01:31.624 --> 00:01:32.926
- Oh yeah!

00:01:32.926 --> 00:01:34.127 align:start size:81% position:19%
Tell you something
right now, man.

00:01:34.127 --> 00:01:36.329
Combat is just a buncha
men in a tight space

00:01:36.329 --> 00:01:37.797 align:start size:84% position:16%
with flashing lights
and loud noises!

00:01:37.797 --> 00:01:39.399
(Peele beatboxing)

00:01:39.399 --> 00:01:41.000
- Just like this!

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:42.502
Yeah, you'll fit
right in at home!

00:01:42.502 --> 00:01:43.703 align:start size:94% position:6%
- It's gon' be great,
man, y'all gonna love it.

00:01:43.703 --> 00:01:44.904
Oh, here it is.

00:01:44.904 --> 00:01:47.207 align:start size:84% position:16%
Can't stop it,
can't stop it, what.

00:01:47.207 --> 00:01:48.041
- Go Krandle.

00:01:48.041 --> 00:01:49.008
Sergeant Krandle.

00:01:49.008 --> 00:01:49.943
Krandle, Krandle, Krandle and

00:01:49.943 --> 00:01:50.777
hold it.

00:01:50.777 --> 00:01:51.611
Hold it.

00:01:51.611 --> 00:01:53.113
And hold it right there.

00:01:53.113 --> 00:01:53.913
- Whoo!

00:01:54.948 --> 00:01:55.915
I'm a robot!

00:01:56.816 --> 00:01:57.784
(Key knocking on stall door)

00:01:57.784 --> 00:01:59.285
Excuse me in there, young man.

00:01:59.285 --> 00:02:00.453 align:start position:0%
Have you ever thought about
joining the United States Army?

00:02:00.453 --> 00:02:02.322
Yes, oh, oh, excuse me.

00:02:02.322 --> 00:02:04.491
I will talk to you
two later, pardon me.

00:02:04.491 --> 00:02:07.694
(helicopter chopping)

00:02:07.694 --> 00:02:10.930
(eerie dramatic music)

00:02:13.533 --> 00:02:14.834
- Decker.

00:02:14.834 --> 00:02:16.369
Agent Jackson,

00:02:16.369 --> 00:02:18.705
you'll be working with
him on this mission.

00:02:18.705 --> 00:02:21.441
- Agent Jackson, let's
get one thing straight,

00:02:21.441 --> 00:02:25.578
I don't like orders and I
don't play by the rules.

00:02:25.578 --> 00:02:27.313
I trust you heard of me?

00:02:27.313 --> 00:02:28.815
- Actually, no I haven't.

00:02:28.815 --> 00:02:29.649
- Ohhh.

00:02:30.583 --> 00:02:31.651
Hubba hubba.

00:02:37.724 --> 00:02:39.025
- We don't have much time.

00:02:39.025 --> 00:02:41.094
The Arachnid agents have
taken over the consult.

00:02:41.094 --> 00:02:44.197
- We need to get you in and
resolve this from the inside.

00:02:45.832 --> 00:02:48.468 align:start size:97% position:3%
We've taken the latest sit-rep
of the hostiles' position

00:02:48.468 --> 00:02:49.802
and we've reconstructed

00:02:49.802 --> 00:02:52.305 align:start size:88% position:13%
a holographic blueprint
of the consulate.

00:02:52.305 --> 00:02:55.642
- Save the mouth squirt for
the new recruits, General.

00:02:57.143 --> 00:03:00.280
Not gonna be impressed by
any fancy, new technology!

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:03.917
(Decker grunting fearfully)

00:03:05.552 --> 00:03:09.022
(Decker breathing hard)

00:03:09.022 --> 00:03:10.790
- It's just a 3D representation.

00:03:12.592 --> 00:03:13.960
Pretty standard these days.

00:03:14.827 --> 00:03:15.662
- Right.

00:03:16.729 --> 00:03:17.964
I know what it is.

00:03:17.964 --> 00:03:19.465
- Agent Jackson,

00:03:19.465 --> 00:03:21.334 align:start size:84% position:16%
you will enter
through this AC duct

00:03:21.334 --> 00:03:22.702
on the south side
of the building.

00:03:22.702 --> 00:03:23.536
- Yes, sir.

00:03:23.536 --> 00:03:24.470
- Decker,

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:25.972
you will be dropped on top

00:03:25.972 --> 00:03:28.675
and then you will gain access
through this elevator shaft.

00:03:28.675 --> 00:03:31.044
We want you to go down
to the fourth floor.

00:03:31.044 --> 00:03:31.878
Make ...

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:34.414
Decker!

00:03:35.848 --> 00:03:37.217
You okay?

00:03:37.217 --> 00:03:38.618
- Heard everything you said.

00:03:40.086 --> 00:03:41.221
Elevator shaft.

00:03:43.656 --> 00:03:44.924
It's bright.

00:03:44.924 --> 00:03:46.559
- Yeah, it's bright.

00:03:46.559 --> 00:03:49.996
The terrorists are located
on the third and fifth floor

00:03:49.996 --> 00:03:51.264
of the building.

00:03:51.264 --> 00:03:52.966
Each floor has six
groups of six men.

00:03:52.966 --> 00:03:54.167
What we're gonna want you to do

00:03:54.167 --> 00:03:55.501 align:start size:84% position:16%
is stop in the
middle of the fourth

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:58.104 align:start size:88% position:13%
and pry open the
elevator door and go ...

00:03:59.572 --> 00:04:01.074 align:start size:94% position:6%
I just want you to move
through that elevator door

00:04:01.074 --> 00:04:02.008
and then go ...

00:04:05.478 --> 00:04:06.312
Pry open ...

00:04:09.515 --> 00:04:11.918
Elevator door and go down
to the third floor ...

00:04:13.586 --> 00:04:14.988 align:start size:84% position:16%
Okay, maybe this
isn't gonna work out.

00:04:14.988 --> 00:04:15.922
- Why?

00:04:15.922 --> 00:04:17.857
What's the matter, General?

00:04:17.857 --> 00:04:20.593 align:start size:88% position:13%
Everybody's putting
their hand in the laser.

00:04:21.494 --> 00:04:23.296
- It's not a laser.

00:04:23.296 --> 00:04:24.897
It's a hologram.

00:04:24.897 --> 00:04:26.399
- Tomato tomato.

00:04:26.399 --> 00:04:30.970 align:start size:97% position:3%
Look, what's with all the
babysitting and handholding?

00:04:30.970 --> 00:04:32.005
Papa's a big boy.

00:04:33.640 --> 00:04:35.475
- Let's zoom into the interior.

00:04:35.475 --> 00:04:37.343
- Yeah, let's zoom in.

00:04:37.343 --> 00:04:40.913
(Decker yelling in shock)

00:04:45.785 --> 00:04:46.986
Let's cut to the chase.

00:04:46.986 --> 00:04:48.121
Why am I here?

00:04:49.555 --> 00:04:52.759
- Your primary target is your
old rival from the Cold War,

00:04:53.760 --> 00:04:56.195
Nikolai Andrekovich.

00:04:56.195 --> 00:04:57.397 align:start size:84% position:16%
Now, Andrekovich
has been leading a -

00:04:57.397 --> 00:04:58.231
- Here's here!

00:04:59.098 --> 00:05:00.433
(Agent Jackson moaning in pain)

00:05:00.433 --> 00:05:01.234
- What?

00:05:01.234 --> 00:05:02.068
Jackson!

00:05:02.068 --> 00:05:02.902
Jackson!

00:05:02.902 --> 00:05:03.736
Dammit.

00:05:05.872 --> 00:05:07.607
(dramatic music)

00:05:07.607 --> 00:05:08.875
Good job, Decker.

00:05:10.610 --> 00:05:13.646 align:start size:94% position:6%
Jackson was an undercover
agent for Arachnid.

00:05:13.646 --> 00:05:15.148
How in the world did you know?

00:05:18.418 --> 00:05:19.819
- Ain't my first rodeo.

00:05:23.589 --> 00:05:25.825
(Decker screaming in pain)

00:05:25.825 --> 00:05:26.659
Hot!

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:30.096
In my day, we made coffee hot.

00:05:32.198 --> 00:05:33.399
- He's here, he's here.

00:05:33.399 --> 00:05:34.701
- Come on, baby, get your sign.

00:05:34.701 --> 00:05:36.002
Brandon, bring the camera.

00:05:36.002 --> 00:05:37.503
Come on, let's go.

00:05:39.706 --> 00:05:42.308
Hold it out, hold it
out right for Daddy,

00:05:42.308 --> 00:05:43.543
so Daddy can see.

00:05:43.543 --> 00:05:44.377
There you go.

00:05:45.345 --> 00:05:46.179
(dog barking)

00:05:46.179 --> 00:05:47.013
- Rocky!

00:05:47.980 --> 00:05:49.549
My boy!

00:05:49.549 --> 00:05:50.750
There's my boy!

00:05:50.750 --> 00:05:51.984 align:start size:84% position:16%
- [Child] He brought
me a teddy bear.

00:05:51.984 --> 00:05:53.853 align:start size:84% position:16%
- [Mom] He did bring
you a teddy bear.

00:05:53.853 --> 00:05:55.254
- Oh my Gosh, look
at this good boy.

00:05:55.254 --> 00:05:56.389
Hey, you want that?

00:05:56.389 --> 00:05:57.256
You want that toy?

00:05:57.256 --> 00:05:58.491
You want that toy?

00:05:58.491 --> 00:05:59.625
- [Child] Why isn't
he coming, Mommy?

00:05:59.625 --> 00:06:00.860 align:start size:84% position:16%
- [Mom] He's
coming, he's coming.

00:06:00.860 --> 00:06:02.962
- [Dad] Oh my Gosh, I
love you so much, Rock.

00:06:02.962 --> 00:06:04.864
Hey, let's go, come on, boy.

00:06:04.864 --> 00:06:07.767
Good dog, good dog, there we go.

00:06:07.767 --> 00:06:10.203
Oh, I missed her so much!

00:06:10.203 --> 00:06:12.038
That's my Rocky!

00:06:12.038 --> 00:06:13.373
That's my Rocky!

00:06:14.874 --> 00:06:18.010
- Gentlemen, it has been
a pleasure and an honor

00:06:18.010 --> 00:06:20.179
to meet you and your people.

00:06:20.179 --> 00:06:23.149
The US government supports
you in every possible way.

00:06:23.149 --> 00:06:24.484 align:start size:84% position:16%
(Ambassador slapping
bug on his head)

00:06:24.484 --> 00:06:27.019
Ideologically, of course.

00:06:27.019 --> 00:06:30.189
However, we cannot offer any
military aid at this time.

00:06:30.189 --> 00:06:32.158 align:start size:84% position:16%
- With all due
respect, Ambassador,

00:06:32.158 --> 00:06:33.593
we need more than that.

00:06:33.593 --> 00:06:36.129 align:start size:97% position:3%
- We are dealing with
terrorism on a daily basis.

00:06:36.129 --> 00:06:37.997
- Oh, that's unfortunate.

00:06:37.997 --> 00:06:40.199
- Warlords overrun villages.

00:06:40.199 --> 00:06:41.667
- Yes, that's regrettable.

00:06:41.667 --> 00:06:43.236
- Rapes, tortures,

00:06:43.236 --> 00:06:45.438
all manner of human atrocity.

00:06:45.438 --> 00:06:46.773
- That's really sad,

00:06:46.773 --> 00:06:49.575
but the US military is
simply spread too thin.

00:06:49.575 --> 00:06:52.078 align:start size:94% position:6%
We can't afford another
intervention at this time.

00:06:53.746 --> 00:06:56.282
- But what we could use
your help with, really,

00:06:56.282 --> 00:06:58.785 align:start size:84% position:16%
is protecting our
vulnerable, plentiful,

00:06:58.785 --> 00:07:01.654 align:start size:84% position:16%
and newly discovered
oil reserves.

00:07:01.654 --> 00:07:03.089
- Oil?

00:07:03.089 --> 00:07:04.056
Excuse me, one second.

00:07:04.056 --> 00:07:05.258
(walkie talkie beeping)

00:07:05.258 --> 00:07:08.127
Operation Golden Eagle is a go.

00:07:08.127 --> 00:07:09.028
(helicopters chopping)

00:07:09.028 --> 00:07:11.264
(people gasping)

00:07:11.264 --> 00:07:13.699
(planes and helicopters roaring)

00:07:13.699 --> 00:07:15.568
Welcome to democracy.

00:07:15.568 --> 00:07:18.571
(war drums beating)

00:07:21.240 --> 00:07:23.776
- We also have natural gases!

00:07:23.776 --> 00:07:24.577
- Oh, yes a lot!

00:07:24.577 --> 00:07:25.411
Lots of it!

00:07:27.079 --> 00:07:29.248
- Commander (indistinct)

00:07:29.248 --> 00:07:31.451
Our forces have been devastated.

00:07:31.451 --> 00:07:33.753
The enemy is at the
edge of the village.

00:07:34.787 --> 00:07:36.889
There are not many of us left.

00:07:36.889 --> 00:07:37.890
Should we surrender?

00:07:41.794 --> 00:07:43.196
- You may surrender, Django,

00:07:45.097 --> 00:07:47.500
but I'm afraid that is a
luxury I cannot afford.

00:07:48.668 --> 00:07:51.170
You have no idea what
they do to warlords.

00:07:51.170 --> 00:07:52.805
If they capture me,

00:07:52.805 --> 00:07:54.340
they will torture me for weeks.

00:07:55.341 --> 00:07:56.509
That is no way to go.

00:07:57.743 --> 00:07:59.178
I want you,

00:07:59.178 --> 00:08:02.415
my most trusted soldier
over the age of eight,

00:08:02.415 --> 00:08:03.516
to take my life.

00:08:04.884 --> 00:08:06.519
That is

00:08:06.519 --> 00:08:07.787
my final order.

00:08:14.293 --> 00:08:15.127
(General screaming)

00:08:15.127 --> 00:08:16.128
(Django stabbing Key)

00:08:16.128 --> 00:08:17.463
(General screaming)

00:08:17.463 --> 00:08:18.397
Stop, stop!

00:08:18.397 --> 00:08:20.199
What the hell are you doing?

00:08:20.199 --> 00:08:22.201
(General screaming)

00:08:22.201 --> 00:08:23.569
- I was trying to kill you, sir.

00:08:23.569 --> 00:08:24.971
- Not with this!

00:08:24.971 --> 00:08:26.272
There's a gun in the drawer!

00:08:26.272 --> 00:08:27.740
(General groaning in pain)

00:08:27.740 --> 00:08:29.308
- Ohhhh.

00:08:29.308 --> 00:08:30.810
So sorry, okay.

00:08:30.810 --> 00:08:32.011
- Amazing.

00:08:32.011 --> 00:08:33.913 align:start size:84% position:16%
You missed every
vital organ, Django.

00:08:35.181 --> 00:08:36.415
- Found it!

00:08:36.415 --> 00:08:38.784
- Alright, now kill me,
Django, hurry, please!

00:08:38.784 --> 00:08:39.619
(gun firing)

00:08:39.619 --> 00:08:43.289
(General screaming)

00:08:43.289 --> 00:08:44.957
Not in the knee!

00:08:44.957 --> 00:08:46.692
- I thought you might
want an open casket.

00:08:46.692 --> 00:08:48.794
- You are an idiot!

00:08:48.794 --> 00:08:50.062
(General groaning in pain)

00:08:50.062 --> 00:08:51.664
- Don't say that,
I did try my best.

00:08:51.664 --> 00:08:53.799
- Shoot me in the
head, you imbecile.

00:08:57.970 --> 00:08:59.005
- Goodbye, Commander.

00:09:00.473 --> 00:09:02.842
You sorry-ass piece of sh -

00:09:02.842 --> 00:09:06.212
(gun clicking)

00:09:06.212 --> 00:09:09.649
- Did you just insult me
as you were about to fire?

00:09:09.649 --> 00:09:10.516
- Oh, well,

00:09:11.417 --> 00:09:13.152
you had insulted me earlier.

00:09:14.820 --> 00:09:16.989
I thought you would be dead.

00:09:16.989 --> 00:09:18.824
Ooh, so sorry.

00:09:18.824 --> 00:09:19.659
- Ow!

00:09:19.659 --> 00:09:20.493
Ow!

00:09:20.493 --> 00:09:21.594
Ow! Ow!

00:09:21.594 --> 00:09:22.528
Stop, stop it!

00:09:22.528 --> 00:09:24.096
What the hell are you doing?

00:09:24.096 --> 00:09:25.364
- Gun is empty.

00:09:25.364 --> 00:09:26.666
Would you like I stab you again?

00:09:26.666 --> 00:09:28.267
- No, no, no, please!

00:09:28.267 --> 00:09:30.069
Django, there are bullets.

00:09:30.069 --> 00:09:31.203
They are over there!

00:09:31.203 --> 00:09:32.572
- Okay.

00:09:32.572 --> 00:09:36.609 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Django, please
hurry, I am in agony!

00:09:36.609 --> 00:09:37.610
(pot hitting General)

00:09:37.610 --> 00:09:39.211
(General screaming)

00:09:39.211 --> 00:09:40.479
What the blazes, man?

00:09:40.479 --> 00:09:42.281
- I thought I could
kill you very quick

00:09:42.281 --> 00:09:44.150
by hitting you with
that big cooking pot.

00:09:44.150 --> 00:09:45.151
- Oh my God, would you please,

00:09:45.151 --> 00:09:46.752
I mean, please get it over with?

00:09:47.987 --> 00:09:49.088
- I did not find the bullets.

00:09:49.088 --> 00:09:49.922
- What?

00:09:49.922 --> 00:09:50.756
- But better,

00:09:50.756 --> 00:09:51.958
boiling hot water.

00:09:51.958 --> 00:09:52.758 align:start size:81% position:19%
- What are you
going to do with -

00:09:52.758 --> 00:09:54.961
(General screaming)

00:09:54.961 --> 00:09:56.195
I surrender!

00:09:56.195 --> 00:09:58.631
I am the General (indistinct)

00:09:58.631 --> 00:10:00.566
- Commander, don't go!

00:10:00.566 --> 00:10:01.767
They'll torture you!

00:10:03.069 --> 00:10:06.906
(dramatic, suspenseful music)

00:10:08.808 --> 00:10:11.544
(birds chirping)

00:10:34.200 --> 00:10:36.802 align:start size:97% position:3%
- I was wondering when I
would come in here to find you

00:10:36.802 --> 00:10:38.037
sitting in that chair.

00:10:40.640 --> 00:10:42.608 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Wasn't easy tracking
you down, Decker.

00:10:44.510 --> 00:10:45.678
- Wasn't supposed to be.

00:10:47.346 --> 00:10:49.382
- I know you've retired, but -

00:10:49.382 --> 00:10:51.751
- That's all behind
me now, General.

00:10:54.387 --> 00:10:57.123 align:start size:88% position:13%
I'm not the man you knew
during the Cold War.

00:10:57.123 --> 00:10:58.224
- I understand.

00:10:59.125 --> 00:11:00.393
We're now facing a threat

00:11:00.393 --> 00:11:02.228
unlike any we've
ever faced before.

00:11:03.162 --> 00:11:04.964
A man with your expertise ...

00:11:04.964 --> 00:11:06.165
- I made a vow

00:11:08.534 --> 00:11:10.603 align:start size:84% position:16%
never to kill
another human being.

00:11:13.973 --> 00:11:15.074
Sorry, General.

00:11:16.575 --> 00:11:18.944
Gonna have to find someone else.

00:11:18.944 --> 00:11:19.779
- Oh.

00:11:21.881 --> 00:11:23.549
No.

00:11:23.549 --> 00:11:25.618
We weren't thinking you'd do it.

00:11:25.618 --> 00:11:26.552
We were

00:11:26.552 --> 00:11:27.953
(General clearing his throat)

00:11:27.953 --> 00:11:29.655 align:start size:97% position:3%
just hoping you could
recommend someone for the job.

00:11:32.425 --> 00:11:34.527 align:start size:84% position:16%
- I guess I could come
out of retirement.

00:11:34.527 --> 00:11:36.028
- No.

00:11:36.028 --> 00:11:37.163
No need.

00:11:37.163 --> 00:11:38.664
Just a recommendation will do.

00:11:38.664 --> 00:11:40.032
- Alright.

00:11:40.032 --> 00:11:41.400
(Decker stabbing table)

00:11:41.400 --> 00:11:42.902
I'll do it.

00:11:42.902 --> 00:11:44.203 align:start size:97% position:3%
- You know, you're just
not what we're looking for.

00:11:44.203 --> 00:11:47.373
- You sly son of a bitch.

00:11:47.373 --> 00:11:50.342
You always knew how
to push my buttons.

00:11:51.477 --> 00:11:52.611
I'm in.

00:11:52.611 --> 00:11:53.446
- Not

00:11:53.446 --> 00:11:54.280
you,

00:11:54.280 --> 00:11:55.114
Decker.

00:11:55.114 --> 00:11:56.415
- Sharp as I ever was,

00:11:57.883 --> 00:11:59.752
even faster too.

00:11:59.752 --> 00:12:00.853
Grab my hand.

00:12:00.853 --> 00:12:01.654
Nope.

00:12:04.056 --> 00:12:05.691
Wait til I count to three first.

00:12:06.625 --> 00:12:07.993
One,

00:12:07.993 --> 00:12:08.961
two,

00:12:08.961 --> 00:12:09.829
three.

00:12:10.996 --> 00:12:12.331
Okay.

00:12:12.331 --> 00:12:13.866
I want you to try and
slap me in the face.

00:12:13.866 --> 00:12:14.900
(General slapping Decker)

00:12:14.900 --> 00:12:16.302
Ohhh, wasn't ready for that.

00:12:18.504 --> 00:12:19.438
Try again.

00:12:19.438 --> 00:12:20.272
(General slapping Decker)

00:12:20.272 --> 00:12:21.574
Okay, you know what?

00:12:22.541 --> 00:12:23.476
- What?

00:12:23.476 --> 00:12:24.910
- Didn't have my adrenaline up

00:12:24.910 --> 00:12:27.913 align:start size:97% position:3%
cause this is not an actual
high stakes situation.

00:12:27.913 --> 00:12:28.748
Alright.

00:12:30.282 --> 00:12:31.117
Draw your weapon.

00:12:32.384 --> 00:12:33.452
And disarmed.

00:12:33.452 --> 00:12:36.122
(gun clicking)

00:12:40.025 --> 00:12:41.026
You're getting pretty quick.

00:12:41.026 --> 00:12:43.095
And disarmed, okay.

00:12:43.095 --> 00:12:44.764
I don't need to
take your weapon.

00:12:47.266 --> 00:12:48.100
You know what?

00:12:49.201 --> 00:12:50.169
Shoot me.

00:12:50.169 --> 00:12:52.338
- I am not going to shoot you.

00:12:52.338 --> 00:12:53.539
- Wing me in the shoulder.

00:12:53.539 --> 00:12:55.007
- This is ridiculous.

00:12:55.007 --> 00:12:56.742
- Try, General.

00:12:56.742 --> 00:12:57.843
See what happens.

00:13:00.246 --> 00:13:01.013
(gun firing)

00:13:01.013 --> 00:13:01.847
Deflected.

00:13:01.847 --> 00:13:02.681
Owwww!

00:13:03.949 --> 00:13:05.785 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Okay, I made a
mistake coming here.

00:13:05.785 --> 00:13:07.086
- Wing me in the other shoulder.

00:13:07.086 --> 00:13:08.120
- I'd rather not.

00:13:08.120 --> 00:13:09.588
- [Decker] I insist.

00:13:09.588 --> 00:13:10.422
(gun firing)

00:13:10.422 --> 00:13:13.793
(Decker screaming)

00:13:13.793 --> 00:13:15.561
That was because my other
arm was already injured.

00:13:15.561 --> 00:13:16.796
- Okay, I'm leaving.

00:13:18.230 --> 00:13:19.165
- Alright.

00:13:19.165 --> 00:13:20.332
All or nothing.

00:13:20.332 --> 00:13:21.233
Gut shot.

00:13:21.233 --> 00:13:22.067
- No!

00:13:22.067 --> 00:13:23.335
- Gut shot, come on!

00:13:23.335 --> 00:13:25.504
If you can shoot me in
the gut, I'll concede.

00:13:25.504 --> 00:13:27.373
- Decker, you have
two wounded arms.

00:13:27.373 --> 00:13:28.240
- Gut shot! Go!

00:13:28.240 --> 00:13:29.074
(gun firing)

00:13:29.074 --> 00:13:30.309
Caught it.

00:13:30.309 --> 00:13:33.779
(Decker groaning weakly)

00:13:33.779 --> 00:13:34.980
- You caught the bullet?

00:13:36.715 --> 00:13:38.083
(Decker groaning weakly)

00:13:38.083 --> 00:13:40.119
So, you're telling
me that the bullet

00:13:40.119 --> 00:13:41.754
is in between your hands

00:13:41.754 --> 00:13:43.088
right now?

00:13:43.088 --> 00:13:45.591
- That's what I'm telling you.

00:13:51.430 --> 00:13:53.766
Is that all you got?

00:13:53.766 --> 00:13:55.134
Come on.

00:13:55.134 --> 00:13:55.935
Head shot.

00:13:56.902 --> 00:13:58.504
(Decker groaning weakly)

00:13:58.504 --> 00:14:00.206
Head shot, let's go.

00:14:00.206 --> 00:14:01.207
I'm ready.

00:14:02.174 --> 00:14:02.975
Wait one second, though.

00:14:02.975 --> 00:14:04.710
(gun firing)

